            "author": "dr.kfazio",
            "region": "US",
            "shares": 4,
            "caption": "I worked out with an AI coach… and I have to admit, this thing is pretty cool. 🤖💪 As a physical therapist, I’m constantly looking at movement quality… not just how much weight someone can lift.  That’s what made the bodypark ATOM so interesting to me. ATOM uses AI powered full body tracking to analyze 34+ skeletal key points while you move.  It can automatically count your reps, give real time feedback on your form, and let you replay your movement afterward so you can actually SEE what your body was doing… One of my favorite features is the movement replay, which allows you to look at things like your movement trajectory and mechanics between sets.  Your post workout reports can also track metrics like range of motion, displacement, velocity, and power over time. Basically… it’s like having an extra set of eyes watching your movement while you train. 👀 I’ve been having a lot of fun testing ATOM and seeing how AI can be incorporated into strength training and movement analysis.  I love that @BodyPark is using technology to make training more interactive, measurable, and educational. Check out the BodyPark ATOM for yourself! The link is in my bio.    #BodyPark #BodyParkatom #atom #FitnessCompanion #fitnessaicoach",
